   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What is on TV?",
     "texto": [
      "Useful verbs: **leer** (a newspaper or magazine), **escuchar** (the radio), **ver** (TV or a series), **navegar por** internet and **buscar** information.\n\nTo say where you saw something you use **en**: lo he leído **en** el periódico; lo he visto **en** la tele; lo he encontrado **en** internet.\n\nTo turn on or off: **poner la tele** or **apagar la tele**. To ask what is on: **¿Qué ponen** esta noche**?**\n\nTo pass on news: **dicen que**… **he leído que**… **he oído que**… After **que** comes a normal sentence: dicen que mañana **hay** tormenta.\n\nTo react: **¿En serio?** **¿De verdad?** **¡No me digas!**"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«En», «dicen que» and «poner»",
     "texto": [
      "Three structures to talk about the media:\n\n- **en** + medium = where you saw it: **en el periódico**, **en la tele**, **en internet**.\n- **dicen que** / **he leído que** + normal sentence: **dicen que hay tormenta**.\n- **poner** for TV: **¿Qué ponen?** (what is on) and **pon la tele** (turn it on).\n\nTo turn it off: **apaga la tele**, and you soften the request with **por favor**."
     ],
